  "content": [
    {
      "text": "bound Isaac his son, and laid him on the altar, Gen. 22:9. let us go … into the wilderness, that we may sacrifice to the Lord, Ex. 3:18. sacrifice of the Lord’s passover, Ex. 12:27. An altar of earth … sacrifice thereon thy … peace offerings, Ex. 20:24 (Lev. 17:5; Deut. 27:7). He that sacrificeth unto any god, save unto the Lord, Ex. 22:20. burnt sacrifice … offer it of his own voluntary will, Lev. 1:3. oblation be a sacrifice of peace offering, Lev. 3:1. law of the sacrifice of peace offerings, Lev. 7:11. any ill blemish, thou shalt not sacrifice it, Deut. 15:21. They sacrificed unto devils, not to God, Deut. 32:17 (1 Cor. 10:20). to obey is better than sacrifice, 1 Sam. 15:22. fire of the Lord … consumed the burnt sacrifice, 1 Kgs. 18:38. That they may offer sacrifices … unto the God, Ezra 6:10. that day they offered great sacrifices, Neh. 12:43. Offer the sacrifices of righteousness, Ps. 4:5. Sacrifice and offering thou didst not desire, Ps. 40:6 (Heb. 10:5). covenant with me by sacrifice, Ps. 50:5. sacrifices of God are a broken spirit, Ps. 51:17. sacrificed their sons and their daughters unto devils, Ps. 106:37. sacrifice of the wicked is an abomination, Prov. 15:8 (21:27). justice and judgment is more acceptable to the Lord than sacrifice, Prov. 21:3. To what purpose is the multitude of your sacrifices, Isa. 1:11. sons and thy daughters … hast thou sacrificed, Ezek. 16:20. shall take away the daily sacrifice, Dan. 11:31. they sacrificed unto Baalim, Hosea 11:2. offered unto me sacrifices and offerings, Amos 5:25 (Acts 7:42). Will the Lord be pleased with thousands of rams, Micah 6:7. Lord hath prepared a sacrifice, Zeph. 1:7. if ye offer the blind for sacrifice, is it not evil, Mal. 1:8.",
